        "13": {
          "id": "13",
          "name": "app_style.md",
          "contents": "# Webpage Style Plan\n\n## Overall Mood\nCalm, supportive, clear, and student-friendly. The page should feel reassuring without feeling childish or clinical.\n\n## Visual Style\nUse a clean modern layout with soft rounded cards, tight spacing, and simple icons or visual placeholders. The design should make the page feel easy to scan during a stressful moment.\n\n\n### Required colors\n- Page background: warm off-white or very light cream\n- Main headings: deep teal\n- Accent color: soft aqua or light blue\n- Body text: dark gray\n- Card backgrounds: white or very pale blue\n\n### Avoid\n- Bright red\n- Neon colors\n- Harsh high-saturation colors\n- Colors that make the page feel like an emergency warning or medical diagnosis tool\n\n## Typography\n\nUse simple, readable typography\n\n### Font style\n- Use a clean sans-serif font.\n- Do not use decorative, handwritten, or novelty fonts.\n\n### Headings\n- Headings should be bold and easy to scan.\n- Use clear size differences between the page title, section headings, and card headings.\n\n### Body text\n- Body text should be easy to read.\n- Use comfortable line spacing.\n- Keep paragraphs short.\n- Use lists when they make information easier to scan.\n\n## Iconography \n\nUse simple inline SVG icons. Do not use external icon libraries, scripts, or imports such as Lucide, Font Awesome, Material Icons, or any other third-party icon set.\n\n### Icon requirements\n- Icons should be created directly in the HTML as inline SVG elements.\n- Use simple line icons or filled shapes.\n- Match the calm, supportive style of the page.\n- Use the accent color or deep teal for icons.\n- Include accessible labels or hidden text when needed.\n\n### Suggested icons\n- Breath strategy: simple air swirl, lungs, or soft wave SVG\n- Move strategy: simple stretching figure, arrow, or motion line SVG\n- Name It strategy: simple pencil, note card, or speech bubble SVG\n\n### Avoid\n- External image links for icons\n- External scripts\n- Icon fonts\n- Overly detailed illustrations\n- Medical or emergency-style symbols\n",
          "folderId": "4",
          "active": false
        },
        "14": {
