          "contents": "# Webpage Style Plan\n\n## Overall Mood\n[[Add 3 or 4 adjectives or short phrases that describe the mood of the page. Examples: calm, energetic, mysterious, trustworthy, playful, dramatic, academic, futuristic, welcoming.]]\n\nThe page should feel [[describe the emotional impression you want the audience to have]]. It should not feel [[describe what the page should avoid feeling like]].\n\n## Visual Style\nUse a [[describe the overall visual style: clean modern layout, magazine-style layout, movie poster style, academic profile, playful card-based layout, etc.]].\n\nThe design should help the audience [[describe what the visual design should help users do: scan quickly, feel excited, understand key ideas, compare information, explore a topic, etc.]].\n\n### Required colors\n- Page background: [[background color or color family]]\n- Main headings: [[heading color]]\n- Accent color: [[accent color]]\n- Body text: [[body text color]]\n- Card or section backgrounds: [[card/section background color]]\n- Optional highlight color: [[optional color for buttons, callouts, or important details]]\n\n### Avoid\n- [[Color, style, or design choice to avoid]]\n- [[Color, style, or design choice to avoid]]\n- [[Color, style, or design choice to avoid]]\n- [[Anything that would make the page feel wrong for the topic or audience]]\n\n## Typography\n\nUse simple, readable typography.\n\n### Font style\n- Use a clean sans-serif font unless the style plan specifically calls for a different readable font.\n- Do not use decorative, handwritten, or novelty fonts unless they clearly match the purpose and remain readable.\n\n### Headings\n- Headings should be bold and easy to scan.\n- Use clear size differences between the page title, section headings, and card headings.\n\n### Body text\n- Body text should be easy to read.\n- Use comfortable line spacing.\n- Keep paragraphs short.\n- Use lists when they make information easier to scan.\n\n## Iconography\n\nUse simple inline SVG icons. Do not use external icon libraries, scripts, or imports such as Lucide, Font Awesome, Material Icons, or any other third-party icon set.\n\n### Suggested Icons\n- [[Shape 1]]\n- [[Shape 2]]\n- [[Shape 3]]",
